[
    {
        "content": "<p>The induction lemma \"<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/TensorProduct/Defs.html#TensorProduct.induction_on\">TensorProduct.induction_on</a>\" has a mathematically redundant \"zero\" step and the following code works fine</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- move this lemma ahead of `induction_on`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zero_tmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗ₜ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sound'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddConGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Rel</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Eqv</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_zero_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">elab_as_elim</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">induction_eliminator</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">induction_on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗ₜ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">motive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">AddCon</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">induction_on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">FreeAddMonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">recOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">convert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCon</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there any reason to keep \"zero\"?</p>",
        "id": 614858536,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1785966001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Dropping it sounds good to me</p>",
        "id": 614859613,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785966584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Redundant.20.22zero.22.20step.20in.20TensorProduct.2Einduction_on/near/614859613\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dropping it sounds good to me</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It also sounds like an unpleasant refactor<span aria-label=\"melting face\" class=\"emoji emoji-1fae0\" role=\"img\" title=\"melting face\">:melting_face:</span> 114 results in 42 files</p>",
        "id": 614859964,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1785966797
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>An LLM would do a great job here. Just saying.</p>",
        "id": 614864708,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785969485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You could do it in two stages:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Define the new induction principle as <code>private induction_on_nozero</code>, prove the current induction_on in terms of it, do the proposed reordring (the math piece). Make the PR, get it merged</li>\n<li>Delete <code>induction_on</code>, rename and make public <code>private induction_on_nozero</code>, and then ask an LLM to delete all the <code>zero</code> branches that are no longer needed</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 614878067,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785975644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Redundant.20.22zero.22.20step.20in.20TensorProduct.2Einduction_on/near/614878067\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You could do it in two stages:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Define the new induction principle as <code>private induction_on_nozero</code>, prove the current induction_on in terms of it, do the proposed reordring (the math piece). Make the PR, get it merged</li>\n<li>Delete <code>induction_on</code>, rename and make public <code>private induction_on_nozero</code>, and then ask an LLM to delete all the <code>zero</code> branches that are no longer needed</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I guess I have some token this cycle to do this. But why do we want a <code>private induction_on_nozero</code> PR first? My plan is to add <code>inductionOn</code> and then put an <code>@[deprecated]</code> on <code>induction_on</code></p>",
        "id": 621982939,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1788663555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyway, here it is <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43481\">#43481</a></p>",
        "id": 622007859,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1788678109
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The purpose of the split was to make it easier to review; since otherwise the diff looks something like</p>\n<ul>\n<li>50 files change to use a new lemma</li>\n<li>hidden in the middle, the actual mathematical / API change</li>\n<li>20 files changed to use the lemma</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 622023737,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788682324
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that this isn't just about PR review; this is also about someone looking through the history to see what change introduced the new version</p>",
        "id": 622023797,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788682395
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Redundant.20.22zero.22.20step.20in.20TensorProduct.2Einduction_on/near/622023797\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that this isn't just about PR review; this is also about someone looking through the history to see what change introduced the new version</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I doubt if there's still a lot of human looking through history trying to identify what got changed manually though...</p>",
        "id": 622024279,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1788682540
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, but using 100x fewer input tokens is probably still of some value</p>",
        "id": 622024372,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788682584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's me <span aria-label=\"raised hand\" class=\"emoji emoji-270b\" role=\"img\" title=\"raised hand\">:raised_hand:</span></p>",
        "id": 622024392,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1788682602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In this case I think the change was small enough that it's not a big deal</p>",
        "id": 622024596,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788682763
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Although I wonder if we could keep the name as <code>induction_on</code> with just the deletion though</p>",
        "id": 622024666,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1788682824
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>inductionOn</code> is the preferred name?</p>",
        "id": 622024989,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788683111
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe this is controversial enough for a separate PR</p>",
        "id": 622025039,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788683157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Loogle suggests we have 2x as many <code>induction_on</code>s as <code>inductionOn</code>, but I think all the ones in core have become <code>inductionOn</code> and so the <code>induction_on</code> spelling is probably a lean3-ism</p>",
        "id": 622025065,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788683177
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"699016\">Edison Xie</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Redundant.20.22zero.22.20step.20in.20TensorProduct.2Einduction_on/near/622024279\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Redundant.20.22zero.22.20step.20in.20TensorProduct.2Einduction_on/near/622023797\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Note that this isn't just about PR review; this is also about someone looking through the history to see what change introduced the new version</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I doubt if there's still a lot of human looking through history trying to identify what got changed manually though...</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I did look at every change history and checked <code>Find all references</code> on <code>induction_on</code> which returned only itself.</p>",
